WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(upbeat music)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.384
- Being a chef for me,

00:00:02.384 --> 00:00:06.551
it's the only thing I could
imagine me doing in my life.

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:09.527
People ask me, what do you
do when you're not cooking?

00:00:09.527 --> 00:00:10.534
Cooking.

00:00:10.534 --> 00:00:13.117
(upbeat music)

00:00:19.307 --> 00:00:22.487
My name is Pam, I'm a chef in Bangkok

00:00:22.487 --> 00:00:26.654
and I have a restaurant in
my home called The Table.

00:00:26.663 --> 00:00:29.290
I cater one table a night.

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:32.985
They can request whatever
they want, no restrictions.

00:00:32.985 --> 00:00:36.075
At first it started off
with the people that I know,

00:00:36.075 --> 00:00:38.681
my friends, my friends of friends,

00:00:38.681 --> 00:00:41.764
the waiting list now is three months.

00:00:44.454 --> 00:00:47.142
Jean Georges is a famous chef,

00:00:47.142 --> 00:00:50.845
and he owns a 3-star Michelin
restaurant in New York,

00:00:50.845 --> 00:00:52.845
which I used to work at.

00:00:54.804 --> 00:00:56.821
I decided to come back to Bangkok

00:00:56.821 --> 00:00:58.765
and open my own restaurant,

00:00:58.765 --> 00:01:01.763
and I didn't open a restaurant.

00:01:01.763 --> 00:01:05.096
Instead I invite people to my own house.

00:01:06.826 --> 00:01:08.660
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:12.720
Today, my guests requests cold crab pasta

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:14.797
and beef Wellington.

00:01:14.797 --> 00:01:17.714
I will go shopping for ingredients.

00:01:19.402 --> 00:01:21.655
I try to focus on local produce.

00:01:21.655 --> 00:01:24.560
(speaking foreign language)

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:28.070
Bangkok is a very special place for a chef

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:32.237
because there is thousand and
thousands of ingredients here.

00:01:32.404 --> 00:01:36.571
And the flavor of each
ingredient is really distinctive.

00:01:36.783 --> 00:01:38.593
And then I will come back home,

00:01:38.593 --> 00:01:40.843
and prepare it a day ahead.

00:01:41.889 --> 00:01:44.452
I usually finish about 80% of the food,

00:01:44.452 --> 00:01:46.670
so when the guests
come, nothing is chaotic

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:48.878
in the kitchen anymore, everything is set.

00:01:48.878 --> 00:01:52.411
(instrumental music)

00:01:52.411 --> 00:01:54.806
I got two helpers in the kitchen,

00:01:54.806 --> 00:01:58.747
and service people for front of the house.

00:01:58.747 --> 00:02:01.997
Everything is clean and ready to serve.

00:02:03.871 --> 00:02:08.038
(speaking foreign language)
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:02:08.229 --> 00:02:10.335
I'm glad that people
see that I'm successful,

00:02:10.335 --> 00:02:14.502
but I don't think that I'm
successful to the top yet.

00:02:14.791 --> 00:02:18.958
If you think you're
successful, you stop learning.

00:02:19.857 --> 00:02:21.138
Being a chef or being a cook,

00:02:21.138 --> 00:02:24.138
you always have to learn new things.

00:02:25.041 --> 00:02:28.883
I just love what I do, I think
it comes out in the food.

00:02:28.883 --> 00:02:30.991
If people come here and they go back

00:02:30.991 --> 00:02:34.658
with smile and full
stomach, I'm just happy.

00:02:36.705 --> 00:02:39.352
Being a chef is not a job for me,

00:02:39.352 --> 00:02:40.884
it's my passion.

00:02:40.884 --> 00:02:41.717
Bye!

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:47.960
(laughing)

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:50.627
(musical tones)

